WEBVTT

00:00:08.320 --> 00:00:11.570
So they're my opponents today, eh?

00:00:11.570 --> 00:00:14.820
I have to give them some fanservice...

00:00:16.200 --> 00:00:18.080
You're as distasteful as always.

00:00:19.240 --> 00:00:22.750
You choose your opponents as your fans and send them off to Hell.

00:00:22.750 --> 00:00:25.670
It's far too much of a hassle to search for a worthy opponent.

00:00:25.670 --> 00:00:27.710
And I do have a ton of fans, you see.

00:00:28.630 --> 00:00:31.210
And <i>every last one</i> of them are terrible Duelists.

00:00:31.210 --> 00:00:34.090
God am I sick of it.

00:00:34.090 --> 00:00:36.590
Collecting Numbers isn't exactly <i>easy</i>, you know.

00:00:38.970 --> 00:00:43.930
Then maybe you'll think to <i>take better care</i> of those Numbers, IV.

00:00:43.930 --> 00:00:49.610
Huh? If you got a problem with the way <i>I'm</i> doing it, why don't you try collecting them <i>yourself</i>, V?

00:00:50.730 --> 00:00:53.570
Now isn't the time for me to act.

00:00:54.360 --> 00:00:58.160
Oh? Are you tryin' to say I'm your <i>pawn</i> or something?

00:00:58.160 --> 00:01:00.410
Then let's settle this here and now...

00:01:01.580 --> 00:01:03.000
Brothers!

00:01:03.790 --> 00:01:07.170
Please stop this! Fighting will do you no good.

00:01:07.170 --> 00:01:09.500
You shut your mouth, III.

00:01:09.500 --> 00:01:11.750
No, III is right.

00:01:14.720 --> 00:01:18.090
IV, you said a bit too much.

00:01:18.090 --> 00:01:22.100
You mustn't forget that noble heart of yours like the other two did.

00:01:22.100 --> 00:01:23.220
Tron...!

00:01:23.220 --> 00:01:25.480
Are you trying to label me as a troublemaker?

00:01:25.890 --> 00:01:27.600
Watch your tongue!

00:01:27.600 --> 00:01:28.520
Say wha-

00:01:30.190 --> 00:01:33.940
I will <i>not</i> tolerate you being rude to Tron!

00:01:36.400 --> 00:01:37.280
Got it...

00:01:37.280 --> 00:01:41.280
III, you understand your role today, do you not?

00:01:41.280 --> 00:01:43.160
I do, Brother V.

00:01:44.370 --> 00:01:48.420
Ryoga Kamishiro is fighting desperately to find IV.

00:01:50.710 --> 00:01:52.960
Give him this Number.

00:01:52.960 --> 00:01:56.800
He is sure to come before you two eventually.

00:01:56.800 --> 00:01:58.680
Yes, Brother V.

00:02:03.680 --> 00:02:05.220
Dr. Faker...

00:02:05.220 --> 00:02:07.890
We will steal everything from him.

00:02:07.890 --> 00:02:11.650
Just as he did us!

00:02:11.650 --> 00:02:12.690
V...

00:02:12.690 --> 00:02:16.940
V, be sure not to let him know of my existence.

00:02:16.940 --> 00:02:20.990
Dr. Faker thinks I'm dead.

00:02:20.990 --> 00:02:24.910
It's <i>my</i> job to notify him of my presence, after all.

00:02:27.330 --> 00:02:31.460
<i>My brave Duelists, good morning!</i>

00:02:31.460 --> 00:02:33.540
<i>It's day two of the World Duel Carnival!</i>

00:02:33.540 --> 00:02:36.630
<i>That's right! Today's where things get real!</i>

00:02:36.630 --> 00:02:39.380
<i>Clash your passionate hearts against one another!</i>

00:02:39.380 --> 00:02:43.010
<i>Heart Burning!</i>

00:02:45.680 --> 00:02:49.310
I'm in top form today!

00:02:49.310 --> 00:02:51.850
<i>Yuma, in top form. How rare.</i>

00:02:51.850 --> 00:02:55.110
Heh! I'm different in this tournament today!

00:02:55.110 --> 00:02:55.860
Check it out!

00:02:56.150 --> 00:02:58.070
<i>What is that? What is that?</i>

00:02:58.070 --> 00:03:00.450
They're Heart Pieces!

00:03:00.450 --> 00:03:01.610
I already got three!

00:03:01.610 --> 00:03:04.580
Let’s follow this momentum and qualify for the Finals!

00:03:04.580 --> 00:03:06.580
I'm gonna bring it to 'em!

00:03:06.580 --> 00:03:08.660
I guess you're a bit overconfident.

00:03:09.080 --> 00:03:10.790
Hurry up already!

00:03:14.670 --> 00:03:16.130
Please wait!

00:03:16.250 --> 00:03:18.710
Tetsuo-<i>kun</i>! And the class rep too!

00:03:18.710 --> 00:03:21.720
They're really energetic too! Nice!

00:03:21.720 --> 00:03:23.550
Hurry up, class rep!

00:03:23.550 --> 00:03:25.510
Please wait-

00:03:28.220 --> 00:03:29.980
That hurt...!

00:03:29.980 --> 00:03:32.440
Hurry it up! We'll be late!

00:03:32.440 --> 00:03:33.310
Hey!

00:03:33.650 --> 00:03:35.440
Why're you guys in such a rush?

00:03:35.440 --> 00:03:36.520
Yuma!

00:03:36.520 --> 00:03:37.230
Listen here!

00:03:37.860 --> 00:03:39.360
To summarize, this is why!

00:03:40.780 --> 00:03:41.570
Who's that dude?

00:03:41.570 --> 00:03:43.610
He's the Asia Champion, IV!

00:03:45.030 --> 00:03:48.620
C'mon! He's the guy Shark fought in the National Championship.

00:03:49.040 --> 00:03:49.830
Shark...

00:03:50.700 --> 00:03:54.500
<i>The guy I once lost to in the National Championship has appeared.</i>

00:03:54.500 --> 00:03:58.960
<i>He... IV, lured me into his trap!</i>

00:03:58.960 --> 00:04:01.420
<i>He even got innocent people involved!</i>

00:04:01.420 --> 00:04:04.890
So this man is the one Shark was talking about.

00:04:04.890 --> 00:04:07.970
We're about to Duel against IV!

00:04:07.970 --> 00:04:09.260
He appointed us!

00:04:09.720 --> 00:04:11.810
Isn't that guy a dangerous opponent?

00:04:11.810 --> 00:04:12.980
Whatever do you mean?

00:04:14.310 --> 00:04:16.940
I heard he used unethical means for victory.

00:04:16.940 --> 00:04:20.030
There isn't a Duelist more gentle than IV.

00:04:20.030 --> 00:04:22.030
To be able to Duel against him...

00:04:22.030 --> 00:04:26.240
To summarize, I already have no regrets in my life!

00:04:26.240 --> 00:04:27.620
We gotta hurry!

00:04:27.620 --> 00:04:29.330
Ah, you're right!

00:04:29.330 --> 00:04:30.240
Let's go!

00:04:30.240 --> 00:04:30.910
Yeah!

00:04:30.910 --> 00:04:32.700
Hey! Wait up!

00:04:42.880 --> 00:04:45.380
You're gonna Duel in a place like this?

00:04:45.380 --> 00:04:50.220
It's such a quiet place, so we should be able to take our time and enjoy our Duel with him.

00:04:50.220 --> 00:04:52.350
Yeah. That's for sure.

00:04:52.350 --> 00:04:54.350
Ah... I suppose that's true.

00:04:57.770 --> 00:04:59.360
That's IV?

00:05:08.490 --> 00:05:09.910
- It's IV!
 - It's IV!

00:05:12.830 --> 00:05:13.870
You're IV-<i>san</i>, aren't you?!

00:05:13.870 --> 00:05:17.210
I apologize for the wait, Todoroki-<i>kun</i>, Takeda-<i>kun</i>.

00:05:17.210 --> 00:05:19.420
Well then, let us get started.

00:05:19.420 --> 00:05:23.130
B-Before that, please autograph this for me!

00:05:23.130 --> 00:05:24.090
Me too, me too!

00:05:24.090 --> 00:05:27.970
With pleasure. Fanservice is my motto, after all.

00:05:29.930 --> 00:05:31.050
Is this acceptable?

00:05:31.850 --> 00:05:33.220
Thank you so much!

00:05:33.220 --> 00:05:34.350
M-Me too!

00:05:35.270 --> 00:05:36.730
Here you go.

00:05:38.480 --> 00:05:39.900
Now for our Duel.

00:05:39.900 --> 00:05:42.860
Tetsuo-<i>kun</i>, who’s going first?

00:05:42.860 --> 00:05:43.900
Oh, right...

00:05:43.900 --> 00:05:46.780
If you'd like, the three of us can go together.

00:05:47.490 --> 00:05:51.450
The rules will be a Battle Royale betting all our Heart Pieces.

00:05:52.410 --> 00:05:54.160
A Battle Royale?

00:05:54.160 --> 00:05:55.450
Is he serious?

00:05:55.910 --> 00:06:01.000
The Battle Royale rules makes it so all participants are enemies.

00:06:01.000 --> 00:06:04.590
But Tetsuo and the class rep will no doubt be aiming for IV.

00:06:04.590 --> 00:06:08.800
In other words, this is actually a 2-on-1 match.

00:06:08.800 --> 00:06:12.510
He may be an advanced player, but these conditions still put him at the absolute disadvantage.

00:06:12.510 --> 00:06:17.310
I want you two to realize the infinite possibilities during a Duel.

00:06:17.310 --> 00:06:19.900
You guys could even defeat me in the process.

00:06:19.900 --> 00:06:22.270
That's what Dueling is all about!

00:06:22.270 --> 00:06:24.860
Wow, IV's a pretty nice dude!

00:06:24.860 --> 00:06:26.070
Here goes!

00:06:26.070 --> 00:06:26.990
Yeah!

00:06:27.740 --> 00:06:29.570
Duel Disk, set!

00:06:41.500 --> 00:06:43.210
D-Gazers, set!

00:06:48.420 --> 00:06:50.630
<i>AR Vision - Link established.</i>

00:06:50.630 --> 00:06:51.800
Duel!!

00:06:53.800 --> 00:06:56.180
<i>The second day of the World Duel Carnival has begun!</i>

00:06:56.180 --> 00:07:02.560
<i>Only those who collect six Heart Pieces can advance to the Finals!</i>

00:07:02.560 --> 00:07:06.860
I'm definitely gonna complete the Heart Puzzle and make it into the Finals!

00:07:08.420 --> 00:07:11.090
<i>As I get closer, I stretch my hand out</i>

00:07:11.090 --> 00:07:14.140
<i>towards that shining light leading towards tomorrow</i>

00:07:14.310 --> 00:07:21.400
<i>I dream of a world that expands from my feet.</i>

00:07:25.150 --> 00:07:30.660
<i>I haven't a clue of where things like dreams and hopes are at.</i>

00:07:30.660 --> 00:07:35.160
<i>Even if I run looking for it, I still can't seem to find it.</i>

00:07:36.120 --> 00:07:41.620
<i>I wonder if I have fallen into a gap of truth and lies.</i>

00:07:41.620 --> 00:07:46.420
<i>Even so, our grand tale has yet to begin.</i>

00:07:46.840 --> 00:07:52.090
<i>Let's move on towards tomorrow, 
even if our road begins to fall apart.</i>

00:07:52.090 --> 00:07:57.350
<i>I will jump forward, before all my
 strength completely drains.</i>

00:07:57.770 --> 00:08:00.230
<i>The closer I get, the further it becomes,</i>

00:08:00.350 --> 00:08:03.520
<i>that truth that I must seize.</i>

00:08:03.520 --> 00:08:08.690
<i>It's to find hope that we desire from a future unseen.</i>

00:08:08.690 --> 00:08:11.280
<i>With a heart stronger than anyone else,</i>

00:08:11.490 --> 00:08:14.450
<i>I'll learn to keep running up.</i>

00:08:14.780 --> 00:08:20.000
<i>With the strength to win any battle, 
despite just how weak I am,</i>

00:08:20.500 --> 00:08:22.500
<i>My purpose is to find,</i>

00:08:22.500 --> 00:08:25.500
<i>with these invaluable friends of mine,</i>

00:08:25.500 --> 00:08:32.300
<i>The future of the world expanding
 from my feet with my own eyes.</i>

00:08:38.200 --> 00:08:40.950
Please, you two go first.

00:08:41.790 --> 00:08:46.250
According to the rules of a Battle Royale, the player with the later gets more of a disadvantage.

00:08:46.250 --> 00:08:48.500
But he actually forfeits going first!

00:08:48.500 --> 00:08:50.050
I'm going first!

00:08:50.050 --> 00:08:54.720
"Number 33: The Hellish Tag Duel!
 The Fiendish Hero, IV"

00:08:50.670 --> 00:08:52.420
My turn! Draw!

00:08:52.420 --> 00:08:55.010
I Summon Aye-Iron!

00:08:59.310 --> 00:09:04.520
The Battle Royale rules state that none of the players can attack in their first turns!

00:09:04.520 --> 00:09:06.690
I end my turn with that!

00:09:07.980 --> 00:09:10.150
My turn! Draw!

00:09:10.150 --> 00:09:13.190
I Summon Debugger X!

00:09:15.700 --> 00:09:17.700
That will end my turn!

00:09:17.700 --> 00:09:21.120
Wow, you guys brought out some unique Monsters!

00:09:21.120 --> 00:09:25.210
That's how it should be. It almost feels like I have no chance.

00:09:25.210 --> 00:09:28.460
Tetsuo-<i>kun</i>, we were praised by IV!

00:09:28.460 --> 00:09:30.590
Yeah! But don't let your guard down.

00:09:30.590 --> 00:09:33.300
My turn! Draw!

00:09:33.300 --> 00:09:36.340
I set a Monster in face-down Defense Mode!

00:09:37.300 --> 00:09:40.640
I then set two cards.

00:09:40.640 --> 00:09:45.350
I activate the Field Magic, Xyz Colosseum, from my hand!

00:09:45.350 --> 00:09:52.900
This card can increases all Xyz Monster’s Attack Power by 200...

00:09:52.900 --> 00:09:56.610
All Monsters other than Xyz Monsters cannot declare an attack.

00:09:58.070 --> 00:10:00.030
And that is the end of my turn.

00:10:02.620 --> 00:10:04.580
A cemetery?

00:10:04.580 --> 00:10:09.460
<i>A Colosseum for Xyz Monsters... Why play such a Field Magic?</i>

00:10:09.460 --> 00:10:14.300
<i>After all, the opponent’s Xyz Monsters will gain Attack Power too.</i>

00:10:14.300 --> 00:10:20.300
In order to Summon an Xyz Monster, 2 or more Monsters with the same level are required.

00:10:20.300 --> 00:10:25.470
Before we have enough Monsters, he is planning to seal our attacks using Xyz Colosseum.

00:10:25.470 --> 00:10:27.390
But that won't work!

00:10:27.390 --> 00:10:29.900
My turn! Draw!

00:10:29.900 --> 00:10:32.520
I Summon Tinplate Goldfish!

00:10:34.820 --> 00:10:41.280
When this card is Summoned successfully, if I have another Tinplate Goldfish in my hand, I can Special Summon it!

00:10:41.280 --> 00:10:44.490
I Special Summon Tinplate Goldfish!

00:10:44.490 --> 00:10:48.120
Now he's got three Level Four Monsters on his field!

00:10:48.120 --> 00:10:49.000
Gonna do it?!

00:10:49.000 --> 00:10:53.920
I Overlay my two Level Four Tinplate Goldfish and my Aye-Iron!

00:10:54.250 --> 00:10:58.050
I build the Overlay Network with my three Monsters!

00:10:58.050 --> 00:10:59.630
Xyz Summon!

00:10:59.630 --> 00:11:03.100
Come forth, Tinplate Archduke!

00:11:08.980 --> 00:11:10.140
Amazing!

00:11:10.140 --> 00:11:12.480
I can't believe you already Summoned an Xyz Monster!

00:11:12.480 --> 00:11:15.480
I activate the effect of Xyz Colosseum!

00:11:15.480 --> 00:11:22.820
Due to this card’s effect, the Xyz Monster, Tinplate Archduke, gains 200 Attack Points!

00:11:22.820 --> 00:11:26.450
Here goes! I activate Tinplate Archduke's effect!

00:11:26.450 --> 00:11:32.210
By detaching one Overlay Unit, I can change the battle position of one of my opponent's Monsters!

00:11:32.210 --> 00:11:35.880
This can't be! All of a sudden, my face-down Monster is...

00:11:35.880 --> 00:11:38.300
What a Duelist you are!

00:11:38.300 --> 00:11:40.130
Th-That so?

00:11:40.130 --> 00:11:45.390
Tetsuo-<i>kun</i>! You got praised by IV again! To summarize, I am envious!

00:11:47.510 --> 00:11:50.310
I switch IV's face-down Defense Monster into Attack Mode!

00:11:50.310 --> 00:11:54.730
The monster I set was Gimmick Puppet - Baby Face!

00:11:54.730 --> 00:11:57.150
A Monster with zero Attack Points...

00:11:57.150 --> 00:11:59.070
This is a good chance!

00:11:59.070 --> 00:12:00.070
I know!

00:12:00.650 --> 00:12:04.370
Tinplate Archduke, attack Gimmick Puppet - Baby Face!

00:12:04.370 --> 00:12:06.080
Strike of the Archduke!!

00:12:11.000 --> 00:12:13.250
I activate the Trap Card, Repair Puppet!

00:12:15.080 --> 00:12:19.800
When a Level Four or lower Puppet Monster was destroyed by battle,

00:12:19.800 --> 00:12:23.220
this card can Special Summon a Monster with the same card name from my deck!

00:12:23.220 --> 00:12:26.260
Come forth, Gimmick Puppet - Baby Face!

00:12:28.760 --> 00:12:31.930
But that Monster's useless against me!

00:12:31.930 --> 00:12:34.560
I activate Tinplate Archduke's effect!

00:12:34.560 --> 00:12:37.270
I detach one Overlay Unit...

00:12:38.440 --> 00:12:41.650
...and change the battle position of my opponent's Monster!

00:12:44.660 --> 00:12:49.870
Excellent! So you can use Tinplate Archduke's effect not once, but countless times per Duel?

00:12:49.870 --> 00:12:51.790
Or maybe I should say, "This is bad."

00:12:51.790 --> 00:12:54.580
Hey, isn't this impressive?

00:12:54.580 --> 00:12:58.790
Yeah! It may be a two-man effort, but they could really beat the Asian champion!

00:12:58.790 --> 00:13:01.510
My turn! Draw!

00:13:01.510 --> 00:13:05.010
Maybe, just maybe...!

00:13:05.010 --> 00:13:07.550
Even IV himself may have let his guard down!

00:13:07.550 --> 00:13:10.760
IV's got a zero-ATK Monster on his field!

00:13:10.760 --> 00:13:14.980
If we attack with a Monster that has 1600 or more Attack Power, we win!

00:13:14.980 --> 00:13:18.190
I Summon Debugger Z!

00:13:19.190 --> 00:13:23.610
When I successfully Summon Debugger Z when I have Debugger X on the field,

00:13:23.610 --> 00:13:27.700
to summarize, I can Special Summon Debugger Y from the deck!

00:13:29.990 --> 00:13:32.950
Oh! You have three Level Three Monsters!

00:13:32.950 --> 00:13:38.130
I Overlay the three Level Three Monsters, Debugger X, Y, and Z!

00:13:39.290 --> 00:13:42.670
I build the Overlay Network with my three Monsters!

00:13:42.670 --> 00:13:44.260
Xyz Summon!

00:13:44.260 --> 00:13:47.130
Show yourself, Vaccinegal!

00:13:48.220 --> 00:13:53.640
Also, because of the effect of Xyz Colosseum, she gains 200 Attack Points!

00:13:54.180 --> 00:13:55.850
Nice one, class rep!

00:13:55.850 --> 00:13:58.230
Go, Vaccinegal!

00:14:00.310 --> 00:14:01.900
Whoa! If this happens...!

00:14:09.870 --> 00:14:10.820
- We did it!
 - We did it!

00:14:10.820 --> 00:14:11.830
Yes!

00:14:14.330 --> 00:14:16.290
We did it, class rep!

00:14:16.290 --> 00:14:18.710
Yes! We defeated IV!

00:14:18.710 --> 00:14:20.790
Wow, that was magnificent.

00:14:21.750 --> 00:14:24.050
Such wonderful attacks.

00:14:24.670 --> 00:14:27.470
But I did not take any damage.

00:14:27.720 --> 00:14:30.720
No way! They destroyed his Monster...

00:14:32.510 --> 00:14:33.930
Wh-Why...?

00:14:34.520 --> 00:14:40.900
So sorry, but I activated the Continuous Trap prior to the attack, Gimmick Box!

00:14:40.900 --> 00:14:45.860
When I am about to receive Battle Damage, this card can negate that damage,

00:14:45.860 --> 00:14:50.820
and the trap Special Summons itself as a Monster Card!

00:14:50.820 --> 00:14:55.330
Additionally, the negated value becomes this guy’s Attack Power!

00:14:55.330 --> 00:14:57.620
Brother, please hurry.

00:14:57.620 --> 00:14:59.790
If they haven't Summoned them during the previous attacks,

00:14:59.790 --> 00:15:02.750
they don't have Numbers at all.

00:15:02.750 --> 00:15:04.210
Numbers?!

00:15:04.210 --> 00:15:07.670
It can't be! Are they also gathering Numbers?!

00:15:07.670 --> 00:15:09.090
I'm aware.

00:15:09.090 --> 00:15:13.640
Guess it's about time... I show them my <i>true</i> fanservice.

00:15:13.640 --> 00:15:15.140
IV-<i>san</i>?

00:15:15.140 --> 00:15:16.890
What're you talking about?

00:15:16.890 --> 00:15:18.850
I shall offer you hope!

00:15:18.850 --> 00:15:20.440
Then snatch it back!

00:15:20.440 --> 00:15:24.110
It's at this moment that human beings make the most beautiful faces.

00:15:24.110 --> 00:15:28.400
To let you have those expressions... that’s my fanservice!

00:15:29.110 --> 00:15:31.110
My turn! Draw!

00:15:31.450 --> 00:15:33.990
Your Dueling was splendid!

00:15:33.990 --> 00:15:36.410
Both your combination and your tactics!

00:15:36.410 --> 00:15:38.250
But despite that...

00:15:38.250 --> 00:15:43.040
In the end, it was no where near the level needed to defeat me!

00:15:43.040 --> 00:15:46.460
I Summon Gimmick Puppet - Scarecrow!

00:15:52.090 --> 00:15:55.470
And then the Magic Card, Level Cross! Activate!

00:15:55.470 --> 00:15:58.930
By sending a card from my hand to the Graveyard,

00:15:58.930 --> 00:16:03.440
I can double the level of one Level Four or lower Monster!

00:16:03.440 --> 00:16:05.940
I hope you thoroughly enjoy the taste...

00:16:08.480 --> 00:16:10.650
...of my fanservice!

00:16:10.650 --> 00:16:14.990
I Overlay my Level Eight Gimmick Box and Scarecrow!

00:16:15.700 --> 00:16:19.330
I build the Overlay Network with my two Monsters!

00:16:19.330 --> 00:16:20.750
Xyz Summon!

00:16:25.380 --> 00:16:26.540
Come before us...

00:16:26.540 --> 00:16:27.920
Number 16!

00:16:37.050 --> 00:16:41.100
The messenger from Hell, the puppet who controls the strings of fate...

00:16:47.860 --> 00:16:50.110
Gimmick Puppet - Giant Killer!

00:16:52.320 --> 00:16:54.030
A-A Number?!

00:16:54.860 --> 00:16:56.700
He had a Number?!

00:16:56.700 --> 00:17:02.450
And then, the effect of Xyz Colosseum raises its Attack Power up 200 points!

00:17:03.750 --> 00:17:07.330
And I activate the effect of Giant Killer!

00:17:09.210 --> 00:17:13.090
By detaching one Overlay Unit...

00:17:14.050 --> 00:17:19.300
Giant Killer can destroy all of my opponent's Xyz Monsters this turn!

00:17:34.530 --> 00:17:41.160
And you take damage equal to the Attack Power of the Monster that was destroyed!

00:17:41.160 --> 00:17:42.200
- What?!
 - What?!

00:17:42.200 --> 00:17:45.710
Tinplate Archduke had 2400 Attack Points!

00:17:46.580 --> 00:17:49.630
Take my fanservice!

00:17:55.840 --> 00:17:56.550
- Tetsuo-<i>kun</i>!
 - Tetsuo!

00:17:59.390 --> 00:18:01.180
Tetsuo-<i>kun</i>...?

00:18:02.970 --> 00:18:04.560
You're next!

00:18:10.860 --> 00:18:13.690
I destroy your Xyz Monster!

00:18:15.440 --> 00:18:19.030
And you take damage equal to the Monster's Attack Power!

00:18:19.870 --> 00:18:20.780
Take this!

00:18:26.790 --> 00:18:27.750
Class rep!

00:18:31.420 --> 00:18:34.460
Fantastic! It's so beautiful!

00:18:34.460 --> 00:18:36.920
Such painful and twisted expressions!

00:18:36.920 --> 00:18:41.390
It shines only during my service!

00:18:45.970 --> 00:18:48.600
And the true fanservice has only just begun!

00:18:48.600 --> 00:18:53.020
I activate the effect of the Gimmick Puppet - Baby Face in my Graveyard!

00:18:53.020 --> 00:18:57.070
When this Monster rests in my Graveyard after being destroyed in battle,

00:18:57.070 --> 00:19:01.570
when the Monsters who destroyed them are also in the Graveyard,

00:19:01.570 --> 00:19:05.290
by reviving the Baby Faces and then Banishing them,

00:19:05.290 --> 00:19:09.750
I can Special Summon Tinplate Archduke and Vaccinegal!

00:19:13.290 --> 00:19:15.380
It took Tetsuo's Monster from the Graveyard!

00:19:19.840 --> 00:19:24.640
At this moment, because of the effect of Xyz Colosseum,

00:19:24.640 --> 00:19:26.770
Tinplate Archduke gains 200 Attack Points!

00:19:26.770 --> 00:19:30.310
I get it! He's using Xyz Colosseum for this purpose!

00:19:30.310 --> 00:19:34.270
Why the heck's he reviving his enemy's Monsters?!

00:19:34.270 --> 00:19:36.360
This is a looped attack!

00:19:36.360 --> 00:19:40.110
You are nothing but puppets controlled by the strings leading to destruction.

00:19:40.110 --> 00:19:43.410
You cannot escape from my control!

00:19:58.000 --> 00:20:00.720
And your Monsters will be destroyed yet again!

00:20:02.880 --> 00:20:04.890
Bask in the pain!

00:20:11.100 --> 00:20:15.440
By pulling his opponent’s Monsters out from the Graveyard, he can launch a loop attack by destroying those Monsters again,

00:20:15.440 --> 00:20:21.360
while inflicting damage equal to destroyed Monster’s Attack Power to the opponents!

00:20:29.750 --> 00:20:30.500
This is cruel!

00:20:31.830 --> 00:20:33.080
Not yet!

00:20:33.750 --> 00:20:37.210
My fanservice hasn't ended!

00:20:37.210 --> 00:20:38.550
Giant Killer!!

00:20:38.550 --> 00:20:41.590
Wait! The match is over!

00:20:41.590 --> 00:20:45.930
Did you not even noticed just how much they were <i>enjoying</i> my fanservice?

00:20:45.930 --> 00:20:48.680
Go, Giant Killer!

00:20:48.680 --> 00:20:50.520
Final Dance!!

00:21:01.820 --> 00:21:02.490
Class rep!

00:21:02.490 --> 00:21:03.570
Tetsuo!

00:21:07.700 --> 00:21:12.160
Are these tombstones all Duelists defeated by IV?!

00:21:12.160 --> 00:21:13.790
Hey, you all right?!

00:21:13.790 --> 00:21:14.540
Hey!

00:21:14.870 --> 00:21:16.670
<i>How brutal!</i>

00:21:18.250 --> 00:21:20.380
Tetsuo! Pull yourself together!

00:21:20.380 --> 00:21:23.510
Forget me... The class rep...

00:21:26.720 --> 00:21:28.090
I can't believe this...

00:21:29.390 --> 00:21:31.600
These guys really admired you!

00:21:31.600 --> 00:21:33.680
So how could you do this?!

00:21:34.940 --> 00:21:37.730
A worthy star gives everything for his fans!

00:21:37.730 --> 00:21:39.020
And I truly mean <i>everything</i>...

00:21:39.020 --> 00:21:40.650
What'd you say?

00:21:40.650 --> 00:21:43.320
IV, I won't forgive you!

00:21:43.320 --> 00:21:44.490
Fight me!

00:21:44.490 --> 00:21:47.110
Are you going to become one of my fans as well?

00:21:56.410 --> 00:21:57.420
Found you!

00:21:58.880 --> 00:22:00.380
Shark!

00:22:02.800 --> 00:22:06.840
Have you forgotten the face of your <i>greatest</i> fan...

00:22:06.840 --> 00:22:09.850
IV!?

00:22:19.900 --> 00:22:23.070
<i>Someone gave me some water.</i>

00:22:23.440 --> 00:22:28.990
<i>So I was able to paint a rainbow with ease.</i>

00:22:30.120 --> 00:22:34.910
<i>I want to become someone perfect.</i>

00:22:35.700 --> 00:22:37.960
<i>But it's very difficult.</i>

00:22:39.080 --> 00:22:41.540
<i>Even with me suffering,</i>

00:22:41.670 --> 00:22:45.630
<i>I can't seem to grasp victory.</i>

00:22:46.510 --> 00:22:48.430
<i>I want to bloom!</i>

00:22:48.970 --> 00:22:52.890
<i>I must be having some kind of weird dream.</i>

00:22:52.890 --> 00:22:55.930
<i>But If I must fulfill this,</i>

00:22:56.430 --> 00:22:59.230
<i>Then I don't mind being laughed at for it.</i>

00:22:59.390 --> 00:23:06.320
<i>Since it's because your limits are decided on your own.</i>

00:23:06.610 --> 00:23:09.360
<i>I'll show it, overcoming it to tomorrow.</i>

00:23:09.610 --> 00:23:13.830
<i>Ah, I'm aiming for the big blue sky.</i>

00:23:14.030 --> 00:23:15.790
<i>For all of its glory.</i>

00:23:15.790 --> 00:23:17.580
<i>The Freesia of Desire.</i>

00:23:19.330 --> 00:23:22.960
<i>All of those countless flower petals</i>

00:23:23.170 --> 00:23:26.000
<i>They came at the expense of</i>

00:23:26.840 --> 00:23:29.590
<i>me being able to reach those heights.</i>

00:23:29.970 --> 00:23:34.010
<i>Ah, even though I lost my way today,</i>

00:23:34.180 --> 00:23:35.850
<i>I still yearn for it.</i>

00:23:35.850 --> 00:23:38.140
<i>That Freesia of Desire.</i>

00:23:41.900 --> 00:23:45.770
After approaching IV, a Duel between III and Shark begins.

00:23:45.770 --> 00:23:48.230
Shark, did you say revenge??

00:23:48.230 --> 00:23:50.280
Who on earth are they?

00:23:50.280 --> 00:23:51.990
Anyhow, we need to get them to the hospital!

00:23:53.110 --> 00:23:55.030
The field's under water?

00:23:55.030 --> 00:23:59.870
Indeed, under these circumstances, there is a way to bring a reversal!! But that’s…

00:23:59.870 --> 00:24:02.330
Next time on Yu-Gi-Oh! ZeXal!

00:24:02.330 --> 00:24:05.670
"The Determined Revenge, Tragic Duelist, Shark"

00:24:05.670 --> 00:24:07.710
I'm gonna bring it to 'em!

00:24:10.920 --> 00:24:13.470
Gosh, Yuma! You farted, didn't you?!

00:24:13.470 --> 00:24:15.930
I-It wasn't me! It was...

00:24:16.810 --> 00:24:18.430
That's right! It was Astral!

00:24:18.430 --> 00:24:20.310
Yuma, what is a fart?

00:24:20.310 --> 00:24:22.100
A fart is he~! He~!

00:24:22.100 --> 00:24:23.140
He~?
